error[Z0401]: `exposure:` of `adjustment_sets` is `u`, which is latent
 --> scripts/main.zeff:6:29
  |
6 | g.adjustment_sets(exposure: u, outcome: b)
  |                             ^ declared `latent` in the graph
  |
  = help: a variable that is not observed has no relation in the data to adjust; if `u` is measured after all, take it out of the `latent` line

error[Z0401]: `outcome:` of `adjustment_sets` is `s`, which is one the data are selected on
 --> scripts/main.zeff:5:41
  |
5 | g.adjustment_sets(exposure: a, outcome: s)
  |                                         ^ declared `selected` in the graph
  |
  = help: the data hold `s` fixed, so they show no relation of it to anything; if `s` varies in the data, take it out of the `selected` line

error[Z0401]: `adjustment_sets` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | dataset(wages).adjustment_sets(exposure: educ, outcome: wage)
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `adjustment_sets` takes a Dag first; `x.adjustment_sets(...)` is `adjustment_sets(x, ...)`

